Author: Jon Shallow <supjps-libcoap@jpshallow.com>
Date:   Mon Feb 7 12:47:13 2022 +0000

    proxy_uri: Fix handling the resource for uri path in Proxy-Uri

    If the server recieving a Proxy request determines that it is the final
    endpoint of the request, the resource that the request was sent to
    was wrong. The update to coap_get_uri_path() fixes this issue.

    There is now also parameter support for the proxy definition for the
    coap-server where any defined host is treated as being the final endpoint
    is in:

      coap-server -P ,

    This allows any actual server to be the final endpoint of any proxy request
    without have to define all the names or IP addresses that the coap-server is
    known by.  Note that if there is nothing following the , (comma), anything
    before the , (comma) will never be used.

    Documentation updated.

